      "text": "Loop scripts used for every rate: /tmp/ft/ev/loop.sh (one test, N runs, B busy-loop CPU burners inside the same heavy scope capped at 6 CPUs), loopbin.sh (whole test binary), maploop.sh (one map recipe). base-release-first ran on c697899, whose codex.rs and release.rs equal main; two later base runs of the same loop at main passed 0/20 and 0/20 (the race needs yardd's reader to get ahead of the task awaiting turn/start, which the burners only sometimes cause), so the deterministic regression test is the real proof."
